      "role": "cite",
      "name": "requirements.sdk.domain",
      "commentary": "An *application domain* is the application's graph, node contents, and evidence\nstorage, made available together for criterion execution. In the SDK, it\nimplements [`Domain`](../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/domain/trait.Domain.html) to supply\nits shared types, node and edge operations, and evidence persistence."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The passage in `md/requirements/sdk.md` (section \"Defining the application domain\") is book commentary that cites `requirements.sdk.domain` with {cite}. That is the right role for prose. It has no {impl} or {test} on the same requirement, so it is not redundant.\n\nIts claims agree with the requirement:\n- The requirement says every application domain implements `trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. The commentary says the same: \"In the SDK, it implements `Domain`\".\n- The requirement says the trait's members are introduced in later chapters. The commentary's list of what `Domain` supplies (shared types, node and edge operations, evidence persistence) matches those chapters. Examples are the `NodeId` and `NodeContent` associated types and `node_content` in the graph chapter, and `store_evidence` in the evidence chapter. The graph-edges chapter also cites `requirements.sdk.domain`.\n- The commentary adds no claim that contradicts the requirement. It does not mention cloneability or sharing, and it does not need to.\n\nNo gap found.",
